  "etymarab": {
    "latin": "KRṮ",
    "kok_maddesi": "Back to library EtymArab KRṮ كرث BP – • HDAL • © SG | 15Oct2024 √KRṮ \"root\" ▪ KRṮ_1 ‘leek’ ↗ kurrāṯ ▪ KRṮ_2 ‘to oppress, depress, distress, worry, trouble s.o.; to concern, affect, move s.o.’ ↗ karaṯa ; ‘to care for, pay attention to, take an interest in ↗ ĭktaraṯa ; ‘disaster, catastrophe’ ↗ kāriṯaẗ ▪ KRṮ_ ‘…’: … ▪ [v1] : The item is quite widely attested throughout NSem (Akk, nHbr, Aram) and Ar, so that Fronzaroli1969 (#6.10) posits a Sem * karaṯ‑ as a common ancestor. Ullmann ( WKAS , based on Zimmern1914) would not exclude an origin in Sum gàraš ˢᵃʳ (Halloran_3.0), but Fronzaroli (ibid., 269) is prob. right in assuming that it was the other way round, i.e., that the Sum word is a borrowing from Sem. – Cf. also the synonymous ↗ qirṭ which, for Fraenkel1886, is perh. from Grk kartón ‘chive’. ▪ [v2] : Etymology obscure. No obvious cognates in other Sem languages. ▪ … ▪ … ▪ DRS 10 (2012) #KRṮ- 1 Akk karaš‑ , nHbr kᵊrēšā , Aram karrātā , Ar kurrāṯ , karrāṯ , MġrAr krāṯ ‘poireau’. – ? YemAr karaṯ : sorte d’euphorbe. - 2 Ar karaṯa ‘angoisser, affliger, troubler, être oppressant pour’ ▪ … ▪ See above, section CONC. ▪ … – – Sources ; meta ; gram ; engl ; conc ; hist ; cogn ; disc ; west ; deriv ;",
    "kelime_maddeleri": []
